From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 09:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Drop the eager engine's config-copy workaround

core/eager_session.plain() deep-converted pose_cfg before handing it to
PoseNetFactory, and again before export_model dumped it to YAML, because
BaseKerasPoseNet stored the config with a plain `self.cfg = cfg` and
tf.keras.Model.__setattr__ rewrote the caller's lists and dicts into
ListWrapper/DictWrapper in place.  Without it export_model died with
"RepresenterError: cannot represent an object: ListWrapper([...])".

That is fixed at source now: BaseKerasPoseNet assigns cfg through
set_untracked(), so Keras never sees the assignment.  Building either Keras
net from a real pose_cfg with no plain() anywhere leaves zero wrappers in the
caller's dict, yaml.dump round-trips it unchanged, and the dump carries no
!!python tags -- through DeepLabCut's own dumper as well as yaml's.

Carrying both mechanisms would not just be redundant, it would be wrong.
PoseMultiNetKeras.__init__ writes cfg["multi_stage"] = multi_stage and
"resnet" in net_type back into the caller's dict, exactly as PoseMultiNet
does, and set_untracked() was written to keep that write-through working --
its commit message says so and there is a test for it.  Handing the factory
plain(cfg) hands it a copy, which silently swallows that write and makes the
Keras net diverge from the tf_slim one.  Nothing in the engine reads
multi_stage after the net is built, so it was latent, but it was the very
divergence the fix went out of its way to avoid.

Re-verified after the removal, against the tf_slim engine: inference on 16
real frames is bit-identical for resnet_50 at batch 1 and for resnet_50 +PAF
at batch 8 (part_prob, locref, pairwise_pred all 0.0e+00, peak indices and
decoded keypoints identical); export_model still resolves every node name,
with concat_1 bit-identical and the multi-animal outputs at 2.7e-07 / 3.0e-06
/ 3.9e-06 and Cast_2 identical; the exported pose_cfg.yaml reloads as a plain
dict with no !!python tags; train_network still runs eagerly end to end and
writes a snapshot the tf_slim graph reads back bit for bit (0.0e+00 on both
part_prob and locref).
---
diff --git a/deeplabcut/pose_estimation_tensorflow/core/eager_session.py b/deeplabcut/pose_estimation_tensorflow/core/eager_session.py
index 1e6fa5c..a77118f 100644
--- a/deeplabcut/pose_estimation_tensorflow/core/eager_session.py
+++ b/deeplabcut/pose_estimation_tensorflow/core/eager_session.py
@@ -29,23 +29,6 @@ import numpy as np
 import tensorflow as tf
 
 
-def plain(value):
-    """Strip Keras's attribute-tracking wrappers out of a config.
-
-    ``BaseKerasPoseNet.__init__`` assigns ``cfg`` to an attribute of a
-    ``tf.keras.Model``, which replaces its lists and dicts with ``ListWrapper``
-    and ``_DictWrapper``.  Those are not YAML serialisable, so writing the
-    exported pose_cfg.yaml fails.  Networks are handed a plain copy and
-    anything on its way back out to YAML is converted back.
-    """
-    if isinstance(value, dict):
-        return {k: plain(v) for k, v in value.items()}
-    if isinstance(value, (list, tuple)):
-        converted = [plain(v) for v in value]
-        return tuple(converted) if isinstance(value, tuple) else converted
-    return value
-
-
 class Fetch:
     """Stands in for a graph tensor in the (sess, inputs, outputs) contract."""
 
diff --git a/deeplabcut/pose_estimation_tensorflow/core/predict.py b/deeplabcut/pose_estimation_tensorflow/core/predict.py
index 99dac18..7148b0f 100644
--- a/deeplabcut/pose_estimation_tensorflow/core/predict.py
+++ b/deeplabcut/pose_estimation_tensorflow/core/predict.py
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@ from deeplabcut.pose_estimation_tensorflow.nnets.factory import (
 )
 
 from . import legacy_tf1
-from .eager_session import EagerSession, Fetch, plain
+from .eager_session import EagerSession, Fetch
 from .train_eager import configure_gpu_memory_growth
 from .openvino.session import OpenVINOSession
 
@@ -31,11 +31,12 @@ from .openvino.session import OpenVINOSession
 def build_eager_net(cfg, trace_batch=1):
     """Build the Keras pose net and restore ``cfg["init_weights"]`` into it.
 
-    The network is handed a plain copy of the config because
-    ``BaseKerasPoseNet`` stores it on a ``tf.keras.Model``, which would replace
-    its lists and dicts with Keras tracking wrappers.
+    ``cfg`` is passed through untouched: ``BaseKerasPoseNet`` stores it with
+    ``set_untracked``, and ``PoseMultiNetKeras`` writes ``cfg["multi_stage"]``
+    back into it the way the tf_slim net does, so it has to be the caller's own
+    dict and not a copy.
     """
-    net = PoseNetFactory.create(plain(cfg), engine=KERAS_ENGINE)
+    net = PoseNetFactory.create(cfg, engine=KERAS_ENGINE)
     net.build_for([trace_batch, 64, 64, 3])
     checkpoint.load_tf1_checkpoint(net, cfg["init_weights"])
     return net
